/* ===========================================================================
 * MUZZLES — where each unit's rounds leave from, as DATA.
 * GENERATED by tools/gen_muzzles.js (round 95). Re-run it only to change the
 * ballistics on purpose; `tools/test_round95.js` checks this file's shape.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The simulation used to read this off the DRAWN model every shot — the barrel
 * tip marker, through the pose engine and the hull rock — so the art decided
 * the ballistics: every model drawn 25% bigger fought a measurably different
 * battle (Cobra: the Breakout, seed 7, 60 s: 1158830616 → -1899692997), and
 * so did one model posed on a different frame, because poses are sampled on a
 * clock set by the camera. `Unit._boreAt` reads this instead, so a unit can be
 * re-drawn — box art, painted cards, a new model — and fight exactly the same.
 *
 * Model frame: x right, y up, z forward, from the unit's `pos` (ground).
 *
 *   p, t   a mounted gun: `p` the turret's pivot in the hull frame, `t` the
 *          muzzle from that pivot in the turret frame, turned by the gun's
 *          traverse (`gunYaw`, or the bearing for a mount that is not laid).
 *          `t` alone: fixed in the hull frame (casemates, mortars, pintles).
 *   s      a man: index into `shapes` — one point per stance (`_stance`), the
 *          pose settled, laid level on a man at forty units, no recoil or sway.
 *          A prone muzzle is below the ground here as it is on the model;
 *          `MUZZLE_FLOOR` lifts it, as it always did.
 *   c, l   crew-served (lies behind the gun) / low-profile (goes flat when
 *          holding) — what the team IS, which the simulation also read off the
 *          drawing (`rig.crewServed`, `rig.lowProfile`).
 *
 * ROUND 97 re-measured twenty-four rows ON PURPOSE: every type now drawn as a
 * Blender scale model (tools/blender/, BAKED_MODELS), whose barrel ends where
 * the real one did — the Panther's L/70 1.16 u further out than the box's, the
 * leIG 18's 0.9 m barrel a metre SHORTER — and the T-34s and the Nashorn,
 * rescaled to the models' 0.75 u/m. Rewritten by tools/set_muzzles.py from
 * GenMuzzles with the models loaded. Every other row, the infantry shapes
 * included, is untouched: the period figures (assets/figures.js) stand 0.065 u
 * taller at the hip, and the rifle rounds were deliberately left leaving from
 * where they always had.
 *
 * ROUND 100 re-measured FIVE rows ON PURPOSE, each with its own new shape (25-
 * 29, appended — no shared index moved): the Bazooka, the Panzerschreck, the
 * PIAT, the PTRD and the Panzerfaust, now scale models hung by where they sit
 * on the shoulder. They had all fired from one built tube's mouth; a real
 * PTRD is two metres long and its round leaves 0.62 u further out, a real
 * Bazooka's 0.39 u nearer. Every other man's weapon became a scale model too
 * and was slid along its bore to keep this table's muzzle, so no other row —
 * the lunge mine's included (it lands within 2 mm) — changed.
 * ======================================================================== */
